  "slug": "inventory-count-inventory-adjustment-form",
  "title": "Inventory Count Inventory Adjustment Form",
  "subtitle": "Reconcile the inventory count source state to verified evidence, explain every variance, control affected inventory, authorize exact postings, and verify the ledger.",
  "description": "An original, fillable inventory count inventory adjustment form for controlling controlled physical inventory count and reconciliation package through inventory adjustment identity, observations, evidence, decision, exceptions, escalation, completion, handoff, and final verification without replacing applicable requirements or professional review.",
  "use_case": "Use when system, first-count, recount, and approved quantity or related identity, location, status, or ownership differs from the system and a controlled adjustment must remain traceable from physical evidence through approval, posting, and after-state verification.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
